ui-design
=========

This plugin is released under the MIT License (see LICENSE). It contains data and
code derived from the works below. This file names each one, says what was taken from
it, and points at the licence that governs it. The origin of individual catalog rows is
recorded in catalog/data/data-provenance.json.

ui-ux-pro-max-skill
  https://github.com/nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill
  Copyright (c) 2024 Next Level Builder. MIT License.
  The catalog data, the search engine and the design-system generator began as a
  plain copy of this project; the copyright and permission notice is carried in LICENSE.
  The installer, the marketplace manifest, the gallery and the demo project were left
  behind, and this plugin's skills, agents, router, checks and packaging are additions.

Phosphor Icons
  https://github.com/phosphor-icons/core (@phosphor-icons/core 2.1.1)
  https://github.com/phosphor-icons/react (@phosphor-icons/react 2.1.10)
  MIT License.
  catalog/data/phosphor-icons-upstream.json is a manifest of icon names, categories,
  tags and import names taken from these packages, and catalog/data/icons.csv curates
  rows that refer to those names. No icon artwork is bundled.

Google Fonts metadata
  https://github.com/google/fonts (revision recorded in
  catalog/data/google-font-licenses.json under source.revision)
  catalog/data/google-fonts.csv and google-font-licenses.json hold family names,
  categories, styles, axes, subsets and designers read from each family's METADATA.pb,
  with curated keywords added. Font files are not bundled. Each family's licence is recorded per family in
  google-font-licenses.json (OFL, Apache-2.0 or the Ubuntu Font Licence), and it is the
  licence of the font, not of this plugin. Eight families are excluded pending licence
  review; they are listed under excludedFamilies in the same file.

Public design and accessibility documentation
  Guidance rows, palettes and rules were written or checked against public
  documentation. The sources are recorded row by row in data-provenance.json, and
  include the W3C Web Content Accessibility Guidelines 2.2 and its Understanding and
  Techniques documents, the WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices Guide, Apple's Human Interface
  Guidelines, Android accessibility documentation, Material 3, Microsoft Fluent 2,
  Shopify Polaris, Adobe Spectrum and IBM Carbon. Their names and marks belong to their
  owners, and citing them here implies no endorsement.

W3C Design Tokens Community Group format
  https://tr.designtokens.org/format/
  The dtcg output format follows this specification. No text or code is copied.

GSAP
  https://gsap.com/
  The motion presets in catalog/data/motion.csv are short snippets that call the GSAP
  API. GSAP itself is not bundled or redistributed; it has its own licence at
  https://gsap.com/standards-license.
